meta-floor-nav — Floor Navigator Yocto layer
=======================================

Custom BitBake recipe append files and patches for the PHYTEC phyBOARD-Pollux
(i.MX8MP) BSP-Yocto-NXP-i.MX8MP-PD24.1.0 development environment.

Compatibility
-------------

The layer declares compatibility with Yocto Scarthgap in conf/layer.conf.
It was loaded successfully by BitBake in the PHYTEC BSP workspace using the
ampliphy-vendor-xwayland distribution and phyboard-pollux-imx8mp-3 machine.

Dependencies and scope
----------------------

* Requires the base Yocto/OE core layer (LAYERDEPENDS in layer.conf).
* The Chromium bbappend targets the matching chromium-ozone-wayland 117.0.5938.132
  recipe from the BSP's meta-browser/meta-chromium layer.
* The gtk+3 bbappend targets the GTK3 recipe used in this BSP and requests X11
  support for PCManFM alongside the existing Wayland use case.
* This layer does not yet package the manually deployed PCManFM runtime,
  menu-cache executables, board desktop launchers, XDG menu or MIME defaults.

Contents
--------

recipes-browser/chromium/
    Chromium 117 GN/native dependency settings and Blink ELOC_PROTO patch.

recipes-gnome/gtk+/
    GTK3 X11 PACKAGECONFIG append used for the XWayland PCManFM setup.

Usage
-----

Configure the matching PHYTEC BSP workspace first, then add the repository layer:

    bitbake-layers add-layer /path/to/floor_navigator_yocto/meta-floor-nav
    bitbake-layers show-layers

In the current local layout, the repository is located at:

    ~/floor_navigator_yocto/github/floor_navigator_yocto

The full hardware/software procedure is documented in the top-level README and
in docs/*.md. The current board's complete installed desktop is not yet
reproduced solely by rebuilding an image from this layer.

